 "notes": "OSQAR LSW experiment. Headline 95% CL limit: pseudoscalar g_Agamma < 3.5e-8 GeV^-1 (scalar < 3.2e-8) for m_A < 2e-4 eV (abstract, Sec V, Fig 6). Reported the pseudoscalar (axion-like) curve as the main AxionPhoton result. Curve reconstructed from the paper own LSW formula: dN/dt proportional to (P_gA)^2 with P_gA = (1/4)(g B L)^2 [(2/qL) sin(qL/2)]^2 (Eqs 3-4), so g_limit(m) = g0 [(2/qL)sin(qL/2)]^(-1/2), q = omega - sqrt(omega^2-m_A^2), omega=2.33 eV (532 nm), L=14.3 m per magnet, g0=3.5e-8 GeV^-1. This reproduces Fig 6: flat to ~2-3e-4 eV then rising with oscillatory nodes (first node ~6.4e-4 eV). Values capped at 2e-6 GeV^-1 (top of plot) near sinc zeros. Not a DM search: no density dependence.",
